# Judged re-ranking: implementation guide

MillionPodcasts search. Prepared 22 September 2026 for the dev team.

This guide covers how to build what the 60-query audit tested: judge a bigger candidate pool with the v1 rubric, fill thin topics, and serve relevant shows ordered by pitchability. Everything here was measured on live `claude.php` results for 60 weak queries. The scores in the audit were hand-scored against the same rubric, so the pilot in step 8 is where you confirm the numbers with the real API judge.

Files in this package:

| File | What it is |
|---|---|
| `implementation.md` | This guide. |
| `rerank.py` | Reference logic: tiering, pool union, AI-tab and fan-out triggers, serve order, name dedupe. No I/O. Port to PHP. |
| `test_rerank.py` | Unit tests for `rerank.py`. They all pass. Port them with the code. |
| `expected-60.csv` | Per-query audit numbers for all 60 queries. Use for the pilot comparison in step 8. |
| `judging-prompt-v1.zip` | Already shared: the judging prompt, harness, and `golden-hotel-500.json`. Unchanged. |

